2. SUPPLY & DEMAND IN THE MARKET

 - In the first half of 2013, AADA is able to maintain a healthy level of u=
tilisation of 96%-100%
   due to slack season program.

 - However, with the entry of CAT and vessel upgrading from SAS/ACE, utilis=
ation level drop to
   78%, 82%, 87% in June, August, Sept.

 - Base on the conference's projection, there will only be a 1-2% growth in=
 AADA trade and
   therefore AADA is anticipating utilisation factor level as follows:

[9332.jpg]

 - Therefore the need to put a slack season program to keep rates at a sust=
ainable level is very obvious.


3. SLACK SEASON PROGRAM (SSP)

 - If everyone could recall, we have already done a short term blank sailin=
gs (wk 38-46) to stabilise the
   market capacity.

    A. Period week 38 =96 42
        The following blank sailings were confirmed :-
        Week 38                 ACE
        Week 39                 CKA
        Week 40                 CKA + AAS-S
        Week 41                 SAS + NEAX
        Week 42                 CAT

   B. Long term slack season program (end Oct - mid July)

      - SSP starts from week 44 and end in week 29 next year.

     [5BD0.jpg]


4. CKA BLANK SAILINGS

  - Similar to the last arrangement, HJS will be securing slots from AANA a=
nd ACE service
    for space support during our blank weeks.

  - Details will be shared with all concerned parties after finalising with=
 other members.

    [A012.jpg]

  - OCT 20 RR of USD 400/T is set and we hope that through this program, it=
 can give a positive impact
    on the implementation.

  - If there are any further questions with regards to slack season program=
, please do not hesitate to contact me directly.
    Thank you.


